<title>GERMANY: German July retail sales up real 2.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>German July retail sales up real 2.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>		 Yr/Yr pct chg   Index    Yr/yr pct chg    Index</p>
<p>		    (real)	(real)     (nominal)     (nominal)</p>
<p>				  (1994=100)		    (1994=100)</p>
<p> Jul 96	    +2.5	  97.0	   +3.5	    98.5</p>
<p> Jun 96	    -4.7	  91.4	   -4.1	    92.8</p>
<p> May 96	    -3.7	  97.8	   -3.0	    99.4</p>
<p> Jul 95	    -0.1	  94.6	   +0.6	    95.2</p>
<p> Jun 95	    +1.3	  95.9	   +2.1	    96.8</p>
<p> May 95	    +5.1	 101.6	   +5.9	   102.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Data are based on a survey of 20,000 businesses based on European Union statistical standards. Figures exclude petrol and vehicle sales.</p>
<p>	     Mth/Mth pct chg   Index  Mth/Mth pct chg    Index</p>
<p>		    (real)	(real)     (nominal)     (nominal)</p>
<p>				  (1994=100)		    (1994=100)</p>
<p> Jul 96	    -1.9	  98.8	   -1.4	   100.3</p>
<p> Jun 96	    +2.4	 100.7	   +2.2	   102.8</p>
<p> May 96	    -1.5	  98.3	   -1.9	    99.6</p>
<p> Jul 95	    -1.3	  99.5	   -1.5	   100.0</p>
<p> Jun 95	    -2.5	 100.8	   -2.3	   101.5</p>
<p> May 95	    +1.9	 103.4	   +1.9	   103.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Month-on-month figures are calendar- and seasonally-adjusted.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
